pleted":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.4.1.stable.mono.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable.mono - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7283) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600X 6-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe documentation for `TileMapLayer` says this about the `changed` signal:\n\n> Emitted when this TileMapLayer's properties changes. This includes modified cells, properties, or changes made to its assigned TileSet.\n\nHowever, the signal is not emitted when changing cells. Changes to other properties cause the signal to be emitted normally.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Download and edit the minimal reproduction project\n2. Edit the `main.tscn` scene\n3. Edit the existing `TileMapLayer` by adding and removing cells in the 2D editor\n4. Look for the message `TileMapLayer changed` in the output panel. It should be printed every time you modify any cells\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test-tilemap-changed.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20663298/test-tilemap-changed.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/re